     * Policy: One request only: no implicit lookup, retry, polling, collision cleanup, file access, returned-URL fetch,
     * restore or rollback. Supplied strings retain their bytes and are encoded once; null optional inputs omit, while
     * false, zero and empty strings stay supplied. No new range, enum, pattern, URL, address-resolution or
     * password-strength validation. Offline contracts do not establish live compatibility.
     *
     * Documented: Requires nova-wordpress plus redirects, wp-toolkit and mysql, an HTTPS source resolving only to
     * public addresses, and an owned destination domain with its own document root. These are server prerequisites; the
     * client does not resolve or fetch the source URL. Source URL/user/password are sensitive and
     * source_user/source_password are body-only.
     *
     * Documented: Omitted overwrite uses upstream default 0; explicit false sends 0, while true can replace an existing
     * installation. passwordType remains a supplied string. The background import can fail after API success. Collision
     * queues nothing; running identifiers are not completion or health. Explicit getTaskProgress(installId) works for
     * API tokens; the SSE path needs an interactive session.
     *
     * API-map identity: uapi:WPX/import_website#POST (wire name import_website).
     *
     * @param string $sourceUrl The URL of the source WordPress site to import.
     * @param string $sourceUser The WordPress username for the source site.
     * @param string $sourcePassword The WordPress user's password for the source site.
     * @param string $domain The destination domain for the import.
     * @param bool|null $overwrite Whether to overwrite an existing WordPress installation at the destination. Null
     *     omits it.
     * @param 'admin'|'application'|null $passwordType The password type supplied in the `source_password` parameter.
     *     Null omits it.
     * @return ImportWebsiteResult
     * @throws ApiException If transport, HTTP, the API envelope outcome, or payload validation fails.
